<title>UK: BOE allots 150 mln stg in outright bills, repo.</title>
<headline>BOE allots 150 mln stg in outright bills, repo.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said that it provided the UK money market with 150 million stg of assistance.</p>
<p>It allotted 37 million stg in bills outright and 113 million stg in 6.25 percent repos to June 16 and 17.</p>
<p>This brought total liquidity provided to the market to 1.6 billion stg. The Bank's forecast for the liquidity shortage at noon was 1.6 billion stg.</p>
</text>
